Subject: [PATCH] Pipeline validation v2: Galarian Zigzagoon shiny palette
 recolor (TEMPORARY TEST CHANGE)

This is the corrected first pipeline-validation change for Dreamstone Ruination.
The previous attempt targeted regular Hoenn Zigzagoon, which is not catchable in
Dreamstone Mysteries.

This patch recolors Galarian Zigzagoon's shiny palette to a distinctive
gold/purple luminance-preserving palette. Galarian Zigzagoon is a starter
option in Dreamstone Mysteries, so it can be readily verified.

Files modified:
  - graphics/pokemon/zigzagoon/galar/shiny.pal (battle sprite)
  - graphics/pokemon/zigzagoon/galar/overworld_shiny.pal (overworld follower sprite)

Verification:
  1. Apply patch
  2. Compile in GenSpark
  3. Start a new game and choose Galarian Zigzagoon as starter (with shiny
     'trick of the light' option), OR encounter/generate a shiny Galarian
     Zigzagoon some other way
  4. Confirm the sprite appears in purple/peach tones rather than its normal
     crimson-with-teal-accents shiny coloring

Galarian Zigzagoon is safely revertable -- this palette is not part of any
planned custom palette work for our project.

REVERT after verification: git revert HEAD
